B.Pn=new A.f_("Larger units work the same way: \ubc31 is 100, \ucc9c is 1,000 and \ub9cc is 10,000. Large numbers are grouped by \ub9cc rather than by thousands, so 100,000 is \uc2ed\ub9cc (10 \xd7 10,000). Don't put \uc77c in front of \uc2ed, \ubc31, \ucc9c or \ub9cc, so 10 is \uc2ed and 100 is \ubc31.")
